                <pb facs="0539" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00 Tacoma/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schuyler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-12T11:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>39. It was recently suggested by Nicaraguan Government that conference be held
                    between Presidents of Nicaragua and Honduras aboard American battleship to
                    discuss border and inter-revolutionary difficulties. Department has secured
                    consent of both Presidents to inclusion of President Melendez in
                        conference.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d148-f1"/> You will accordingly invite
                    President Melendez to take part in the conference to be held, if possible,
                    during the coming week aboard the <hi rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi> in Fonseca
                    Bay. You and the Ministers in Honduras and Nicaragua will also be present.
                    Present plans are for <hi rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi> to proceed to Corinto
                    take aboard President Chamorro and proceed to some point between Amapala and La
                    Union readily accessible to both ports. Arrangements being made by Legation
                    Managua. You should inform it as well as Department of President’s acceptance.
                    The Department expects Salvadorean Government will maintain quiet and order
                    until the conference takes place.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
